# Docker (per app)

Each repo is **independent**. Never require a monorepo root compose or bringing api+web+admin up together.

| App | Folder | Up command |
|-----|--------|------------|
| Backend | `nestjs-vz` | `docker compose up -d --build` |
| Frontend | `frontend-vz` | `docker compose up -d --build` |
| Admin | `Admin` | `docker compose up -d --build` |

## Required per app (keep simple)

- Multi-stage `Dockerfile`, pinned tags (no `latest`)
- Non-root `USER`, `HEALTHCHECK`, `npm ci`
- `.dockerignore` excludes `.env*`, `node_modules`, `.git`
- Own `docker-compose.yml` + `.env.example` in that folder
- Secrets only via `.env` / `env_file` — never baked into image

## Frontend / Admin

- Vite build → `nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged` on `8080`
- `VITE_*` as build `ARG` only; `VITE_USE_MOCK=false`
- `nginx.conf` with SPA `try_files` + `/healthz`
- Admin: `X-Frame-Options DENY`

## Backend

- `node:24-alpine`, migrate one-off then `api`
- Postgres in the **same** compose (that app only)
- `SWAGGER_ENABLED=false` in compose for prod profile/default

## Forbidden

- Root `vazinedalat/docker-compose.yml` that couples all apps
- Mandatory Caddy / edge / multi-network setup for local or simple deploy
- `npm install`, secrets in `ARG`/`ENV`, run as root

Follow skill `.cursor/skills/dockerize-production/SKILL.md` when writing/editing Docker files.

